[6979]="700544A0\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tSecure the tower\tSecure the tower. It is recommended to have the quest Into the Dead City underway.\n3\tTalk to one of the Rangers\tTalk to one of the Rangers.\n",
[6980]="70071BC7\n1\tSave Mêshaget\tMêshaget is being attacked by a dwarf-wight! You should help him defeat his foe.\n2\tTalk to Mêshaget\tYou helped Mêshaget and defeated the dwarf-wight he was fighting. You should talk to him.\n3\tSearch the tomb with Mêshaget\tHelp Mêshaget search the tomb for the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding.\n4\tOpen the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding\tThis prominent stone grave must belong to Semayâti the Unyielding. You should open it and see what awaits inside.\n5\tTake the journal\tYou have found the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding, the famous engineer from Lâkindar of old. You should take the journal out of her stone resting place.\n6\tTalk to Mêshaget\tYou have the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding, the famous engineer from Lâkindar of old. You should talk to Mêshaget.\n7\tEscape the Quelling-house with Mêshaget\tYou have what you came for and should now leave the Quelling-house.\n",
[6981]="700000D6\n1\tApproach the old man who stands near (Move forward by pressing W)\tA wizened old man stands before you as you go on your way to the Silver Deep Mine. You should walk towards him.\n2\tTalk to the wizard (Right-click on Gandalf to interact)\tThe wizard Gandalf the Grey, advisor of Thorin Oakenshield, wishes to have a word with you. As Thorin is the master of these halls, you think it best to listen.\n3\tWalk with Gandalf and listen to him for a bit (Move forward by pressing W; A and D to turn)\tYou should accompany Gandalf, for he is a respected advisor of Thorin's.\n4\tFollow Gandalf and listen to his musings\tWalk with Gandalf while he wishes to have you near him.\n5\tTalk to Gormr, the new Steward of Thorin's Hall\tGormr Doursmith has been appointed Steward of Thorin's Halls while Thorin is away. Now that Thorin and Gandalf have departed, you should speak with Gormr to hear his instructions.\n6\tCollect your equipment from the satchel near the door (Right-click on glowing items to loot)\tA satchel full of equipment lies near the entrance to the Silver Deep Mine. You should loot the satchel to equip what you will need for the day's work.\n7\tCollect your equipment from the satchel near the door (Right-click on glowing items to loot)\tA satchel full of equipment lies near the entrance to the Silver Deep Mine. You should loot the satchel to equip what you will need for the day's work.\n8\tTalk to Gimli to find out what to do\tAfter you collected your weapon, a great quaking shook the very mountain above you. Gimli son of Glóin and Gormr are startled.\n9\tSpar with Gimli to practice your skill in battle Be sure to equip your weapon\tGimli wishes for you to prove your strength before he allows you to follow him into the mine to rescue the workers. You never know what evils may appear when the mountains tremble.\n10\tAsk Gimli what to do next\tThe entrance to the Silver Deep Mine stands before you. Gimli wishes to meet you inside the unstable mine, where you will help him get the miners out. You should walk into the doorway.\n11\tTalk to Foreman Otur\tThe miners can be found throughout the mine, hard at work. A quaking of the earth has troubled Gormr, the new leader. He and Gimli want this mine clear so that nobody gets hurt.\n12\tTalk to Foreman Otur\tFollow Foreman Otur to get help for Gimli. While you were trying to call Tvistur to Thorin's ceremony, he broke through a wall, unleashing a troll. The troll slew him, then chased after Gimli. You should follow Otur and see how you can get help for Gimli.\n13\tFollow the tunnel opened by Tvistur to try to get to Gimli\tThe new tunnel excavated by Tvistur now yawns before you. You should go down the tunnel to try to head off the troll as it pursues Gimli.\n14\tExamine the corpse in the Elf-ruins\tYou seem to have uncovered some old ruins, apparently from ancient Elf-structures. A body lies among them.\n15\tDefeat cave-claws as you make your way to Gimli and the troll (total: 5)\tFight your way deeper into the Silver Deep to help Gimli. As you followed Otur, he discovered that the door that led to the bridge had been damaged by the troll's attacks. He asked you to go and help Gimli while he went off to get more help.\n16\tSearch for Gimli\tYou have made your way to Gimli. Help him, if you can!\n17\tTalk to Gandalf\tGandalf the Grey, a wizard accompanying Thorin's Company, saved Gimli from the troll.\n18\tTalk to Gandalf\tGandalf the Grey, a wizard accompanying Thorin's Company, saved Gimli from the troll.\n",
[6982]="7003A670\n1\tJoin Calin and Arnwi at the table nearby\tCalin arrived shortly before you did and joined Arnwi who was waiting at a table nearby.\n2\tObserve the discussion between Arnwi and Calin\tArnwi and Calin have much to catch up on. It is unclear what Arnwi has been up to as he has not been seen by Calin or Herubrand for some time.\n3\tSurvive the Dunlending ambush\tDunlending ruffians heard the sound of commotion and entered the tavern to aid Arnwi.\n4\tSee to Calin's injuries\tAfter the battle Calin is laying very still where he fell. Arnwi caught him off guard with a strong blow that would have killed most men.\n5\tComplete\tAfter the battle Calin is laying very still where he fell. Arnwi caught him off guard with a strong blow that would have killed most men.\n",
[6983]="7006A1D7\n1\tDefeat Krizhmûl\tDefeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.\n2\tDefeat Urâbaz the Mighty\tSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....\n3\tDefeat Raghârik\tThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.\n",
